from pathlib import Path
import re
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]/'working_R4/source/main.tex';s=p.read_text()
abstract=r'''We establish training-derived conditions that certify or exclude nearest-prototype agreement in Gaussian radial basis function classifiers over continuous bandwidth--penalty regions. A class-wise residual decomposition, prototype-block spectral floor, and exact penalty envelope certify complete regions $(0,t]\times[\lambda_0,\infty)$. A strict competing vote in the large-penalty limit supplies a finite disagreement bound, and a signed interval construction certifies local bandwidth bands with finite penalty floors. A frozen MNIST and Fashion-MNIST study spans five seeds and 50--200 prototypes. Immediately beyond the sufficient frontier, more than 99.5\% of query--region pairs remain unresolved. At the median-distance bandwidth scale, the original witness union excludes 88.10\% and 84.48\% of queries, respectively. Local bands at half this scale certify 16.88\% and 40.09\% at ten times the endpoint Gram-matrix norm. Matched-coverage class analysis reveals concentrated predictions within some certified subsets. Across all 30 dataset--seed--budget groups, 328 readouts retain at least 95\% of their group's best validation accuracy; all have zero full-width certificate coverage. Exhaustive reconstruction of 3,366,480 query--width paths identifies 190,405 returns to agreement after sampled disagreement. Expanded finite probes recover at least 95\% of the original limiting-witness cases after mean 15.6 and 20.2 checks at the median-distance scale. These results establish computable continuous decision-persistence guarantees and characterize their empirical separation from competitive prediction, finite-path behavior, and selected-set correctness.'''
s=re.sub(r'\\begin\{abstract\}.*?\\end\{abstract\}',lambda _:r'\begin{abstract}'+'\n'+abstract+'\n'+r'\end{abstract}',s,flags=re.S)
old='Experiments on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST show that the loss of sufficient certification occurs well before widespread identified failures of the requested family, and that local width bands admit additional agreement guarantees at large penalties.'
new='Experiments on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST show that sufficient certification disappears before widespread identified failures of the requested family, local width bands admit additional guarantees at large penalties, and all 328 archived readouts meeting the 95\\% validation-competitive rule have zero full-width coverage. The analysis therefore locates both the guaranteed persistence regions and their empirical separation from high-accuracy operating points.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
old='These comparisons connect the parameter-family guarantees to the behavior and accuracy of finite readouts. Figure~\\ref{fig:paths} introduces the two decisions whose equality is studied.'
new='Class-balanced selection diagnostics identify which queries and classes account for certified-subset accuracy. Exhaustive reconstruction of all 30 original groups then measures observed penalty-path reversals, validation-competitive coverage, and stability across prototype budgets and seeds. A fixed-order replay identifies how finite exclusions accumulate relative to limiting witnesses. Figure~\\ref{fig:paths} introduces the two decisions whose equality is studied.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
s=s.replace('The new diagnostic separates two empirical phenomena.','The region diagnostic separates two empirical phenomena.')
old='The validation comparison places these sufficient bounds far beyond the competitive sampled penalties. It locates the guaranteed reversal along the path, with the first empirical crossing remaining a separate quantity.'
new='The validation comparison places these sufficient bounds far beyond the competitive sampled penalties. The complete archived paths exhibit both earlier finite disagreements and later returns to agreement, including five alternating signs across six penalties. This distinguishes a guaranteed disagreement tail from the observed sequence of finite decisions.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
old='These measurements identify the positive analytical result as a guarantee of persistence across a continuous band and penalty tail, with selected-set composition determining the observed accuracy.'
new='The class-specific reconstruction makes this composition explicit: the MNIST certified subset at that endpoint has 10\\% selected-class macro accuracy across ten represented true classes. On Fashion-MNIST, the stronger selector distributes correct accepted predictions across more classes and selects substantially different queries at equal coverage. These measurements separate continuous persistence, selected-subset accuracy, and class-balanced retention.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
old='The limiting calculation provides a training-derived route to the exclusion; finite readouts can expose many of the same disagreements.'
new='The limiting calculation provides a training-derived route to the exclusion; finite readouts expose many of the same disagreements. The fixed replay order sharpens this comparison: expanded high-penalty probes recover at least 95\\% of the original limiting-witness cases within mean 15.6 and 20.2 checks at $t=s_C$, whereas the original finite probes fail to reach that target in every seed.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
needle='These results connect established RBF and parameter-path analyses through a specific decision-region object.'
insert='The validation-selected analysis supplies a direct empirical answer about competitive operation. Every model retained by each of the fixed 90\\%, 95\\%, and 99\\% rules has zero sharp full-width coverage. The selected models improve accuracy and cross-seed prediction stability as prototype budget increases, while the full-width certificate remains empty. Thus improved finite-model prediction and certified family persistence follow distinct empirical patterns in the archived grid. The broad region exclusions additionally show that many competitive endpoints belong to families containing a strict nearest-label disagreement.\n\n'
assert needle in s;s=s.replace(needle,insert+needle)
start=s.index('\\section{Conclusion}');end=s.index('\\section{Limitations}',start)
s=s[:start]+r'''\section{Conclusion}
Training-derived quantities can both certify and exclude nearest-prototype agreement in Gaussian ridge RBF families. A class-wise residual, spectral floor, and exact penalty envelope certify complete regions $(0,t]\times[\lambda_0,\infty)$. A strict competing vote in the large-penalty limit excludes such a region and supplies a finite disagreement threshold. A signed interval bound additionally certifies local bands $[s,t]\times[\Lambda,\infty)$. The two-dataset evidence separates the early loss of sufficient certification, broad-width incompatibility, and positive local-tail coverage. All 328 validation-competitive models under the primary rule have zero full-width coverage; the finite paths exhibit earlier disagreements and subsequent returns to agreement. Exact witness unions and fixed-order replay quantify the relation between analytical exclusions and finite checks. Class-balanced matched-selection diagnostics explain the observed subset accuracy. The contribution is a computable analysis of continuous decision persistence with certified, excluded, and unresolved outputs, accompanied by an exhaustive assessment of its reach in the archived model families. Tighter signed bounds and alternative region geometries provide concrete routes for studying the unresolved frontier.

'''+s[end:]
old='Two ten-class image datasets and randomly selected prototype subsets determine the empirical scope. The diagnostic, local-tail, validation-reference, and selector analyses are post hoc and use the ten $K=100$ groups. The 95\\% competitive rule describes the archived validation grid, and the sufficient reversal bound supplies an upper threshold for guaranteed disagreement rather than an estimate of its first onset. The selector comparisons describe the fixed endpoint models and sample; a predictive or model-selection benefit at competitive penalties remains an open empirical requirement.'
new='Two ten-class image datasets and randomly selected prototype subsets determine the empirical scope. The post hoc diagnostic, local-tail, reversal-bound, selector, and ordered-probe analyses use the ten $K=100$ groups. Finite-path, validation-competitive, and budget-stability analyses use all 30 original groups. The 90/95/99\\% rules describe relative validation accuracy within the archived grid. Sampled first-detection brackets do not identify unique or earliest continuous crossings, and all-sample agreement does not certify unsampled penalties. The sufficient reversal bound supplies an upper threshold for guaranteed disagreement. Ordered-probe prefix counts measure retrospective set recovery; they supply neither a prospective stopping guarantee nor a measured computational speedup. The selector comparisons describe the fixed endpoint models and sample. No predictive or model-selection improvement is established by the certificates.'
assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)
